From 6984b8c07e84b0cf528243db1838dade971ff513 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:36:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] config: build udmabuf and the system dma-buf heap into
 the Aurora kernel

Local AI runtimes need GPU-visible host memory without a copy. Honeykrisp
already imports dma-bufs. The kernel config did not offer a way to make one
from ordinary pages: CONFIG_UDMABUF and CONFIG_DMABUF_HEAPS were off.

Enable CONFIG_UDMABUF, CONFIG_DMABUF_HEAPS and CONFIG_DMABUF_HEAPS_SYSTEM,
all built in. A memfd then becomes a dma-buf through /dev/udmabuf, and the
GPU driver imports it without a staging copy.

No driver code changes. The change adds three lines to the arm64 config fragment.
---
 arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config b/arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config
index 1e05c59146c1fa..f0030c98cfac40 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config
@@ -45,6 +45,9 @@ CONFIG_DRM_APPLE_AUDIO=y
 CONFIG_DRM_ACCEL=y
 CONFIG_DRM_ACCEL_ANE=m
 CONFIG_DRM_SIMPLEDRM=y
+CONFIG_UDMABUF=y
+CONFIG_DMABUF_HEAPS=y
+CONFIG_DMABUF_HEAPS_SYSTEM=y
 CONFIG_SND_SOC_APPLE_AOP_AUDIO=m
 CONFIG_SND_SOC_APPLE_T8140_AOP_AUDIO=m
 CONFIG_SND_SOC_APPLE_MCA=m

